    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nAfter commit 2c15984ed5b5a6ba59efb0132b6d2889f2904462, `opts` started being copied with `vim.tbl_map` (via [this code path](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ff8b3580935818ef2f21bdd651f057a2ae071eab/lua/mini/pick.lua#L2145)). As a result, it seems that metatables attached to tables inside `opts` are now being stripped during the copy.\n\nRef: aznhe21/actions-preview.nvim#75\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\n-- in lua/mini/pick.lua\nlocal tbl = {}\nsetmetatable(tbl, { __index = {} })\nprint(getmetatable(tbl))                -- table: 0x78b18f265730\nprint(getmetatable(H.copy_tables(tbl))) -- nil\n```",
